    "body": "## Summary\n- route explicit job-publication cancellation through a dedicated coordinator\n- after local cancellation and idempotent wallet-reservation release commit, best-effort cancel any attached Stripe PaymentIntent that is still in a cancellable provider state\n- never let Stripe cleanup failure roll back or invalidate local cancellation; the existing signed-webhook late-payment recovery remains authoritative for races\n- skip provider cancellation for terminal `succeeded` / `canceled` intents\n- add regression coverage for the provider-state allowlist\n\n## Financial / security invariants\n- local publication cancellation remains authoritative and continues to restore `JOB_PUBLICATION_RESERVE` only through the existing idempotent `JOB_PUBLICATION_RELEASE` ledger operation\n- no browser state or Stripe cancellation response mutates wallet/escrow balances\n- a Stripe race that succeeds before cancellation reaches the provider is still handled by the existing signed webhook and late-payment recovery path\n- no PaymentIntent client secret or job payload is persisted or exposed by this slice\n- no schema change / Flyway migration required\n\n## Validation\nDo not merge until all latest-head required CI/checks complete successfully. Any failure will be fixed on this branch and revalidated.",
